<title>FINLAND: FINNISH JAN-JULY TIMBER CUTTINGS DOWN 17 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>FINNISH JAN-JULY TIMBER CUTTINGS DOWN 17 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raw timber market cuttings fell 17 percent year-on-year in January-July to 24.2 million cubic metres, the Finnish Forest Research Institute (METLA) said in a report on Thursday.</p>
<p>Market cuttings of pulpwood fell to 12.9 million cubic metres from 15.1 million in the first eight months last year and logwood cuttings fell to 11.3 million cubic metres from 13.9 million, METLA said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
